# Intendfile — Design intent declarations for tlaiser
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>

@abstract:
What tlaiser INTENDS to become. These are bespoke design goals
specific to the State machine extraction and formal model checking domain.
@end

## Domain-Specific Intent

### live-model-checking\n- description: Continuous model checking as code changes (CI integration)\n- target: Incremental TLC runs on diff\n- status: aspiration\n\n### counterexample-replay\n- description: Turn TLC counterexamples into executable test cases\n- target: Automatic regression tests from spec violations\n- status: aspiration

## Cross-Cutting Intent

### iser-ecosystem-compatibility
- description: Must interoperate with other -iser projects via shared ABI
- target: Idris2 ABI + Zig FFI standard interface
- status: in-progress

### proven-integration
- description: All formal proofs should be verifiable by the proven framework
- target: Integration with hyperpolymath/proven
- status: aspiration
